# === arms ===

# Two checkouts of the same commit.
KOMODO_REPO=/absolute/path/to/vivarium-komodo
TUATARA_REPO=/absolute/path/to/vivarium-tuatara

# One container per arm — this is the isolation. Start them with
# scripts/arm-run.sh. Unset only for a throwaway smoke test.
KOMODO_CONTAINER=vivarium-komodo
TUATARA_CONTAINER=vivarium-tuatara

# Each arm's GitHub identity when it opens PRs.
KOMODO_GH_TOKEN=ghp_...
TUATARA_GH_TOKEN=ghp_...

# Where each arm's transcripts land on the host. Default ~/.vivarium/<container>.
# KOMODO_CODEX_HOME=/absolute/path/to/.vivarium/vivarium-komodo
# TUATARA_CODEX_HOME=/absolute/path/to/.vivarium/vivarium-tuatara

# Host port for each arm's screen (noVNC), published on 127.0.0.1 only. Two
# containers cannot share one, so these must differ — the only per-arm value
# here the arms themselves cannot observe. Open http://127.0.0.1:<port>/vnc.html
# to watch that arm's browser. Defaults 6080 / 6081.
# KOMODO_NOVNC_PORT=6080
# TUATARA_NOVNC_PORT=6081

# === the arms' environment ===
# Run-wide and identical for both arms — this is the controlled environment, not
# per-arm configuration. Read by scripts/arm-run.sh.

# The arm's own nested Docker engine (never the host's socket — that would let
# either arm read the other's checkout and this file). Needs --privileged, which
# arm-run.sh adds. Set 0 for a smoke test on a host that will not allow it.
# VIVARIUM_DOCKER=1

# The X display, window manager and VNC/noVNC the arm's chromium draws on.
# VIVARIUM_GUI=1
# VIVARIUM_SCREEN=1440x900x24

# Image used by arm-run.sh and Greg's ephemeral planner container.
# VIVARIUM_IMAGE=vivarium-arm

# Unset: containers get danger-full-access, host arms workspace-write.
# CODEX_SANDBOX=danger-full-access

# Where codex sessions live. Default ~/.codex.
# CODEX_HOME=/absolute/path/to/.codex

# Abort an arm after this much event silence. Default 240000; 0 disables.
# IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=240000

# === review ===
# The one asymmetry in the experiment: exactly one arm answers this reviewer.

# The login the reviewed arm must answer to. Default greptile-apps[bot].
# GREPTILE_BOT_LOGIN=greptile-apps[bot]

# Max review -> answer -> re-review rounds per pull request. Default 5. A
# maximum, not a count: the loop stops at the first round the reviewer adds
# nothing new, so a pull request that settles early costs one round.
# REVIEW_ROUNDS=5

# How long one round waits for the reviewer before merging unreviewed, and how
# often it looks. Defaults 3600000 / 30000. Only the final, unanswered round
# pays the full timeout. Keep REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MS in step with POLL_TIMEOUT in
# scripts/mirror_sync.sh, or the two arms' reviews are collected on different
# deadlines.
# REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MS=3600000
# REVIEW_POLL_MS=30000
# Reviewer activity is also batched until one fixed 30-second quiet interval
# passes, preventing one submitted review from creating several Codex turns.
